  {
    "shortlink": "https://www.w3.org/TR/wot-security/",
    "description": "<p>This document provides non-normative guidance on Web of Things (WoT) security and privacy. The Web of Things is descriptive, not prescriptive, and so is generally designed to support the security models and mechanisms of the systems it describes, not introduce new ones. However, a WoT system also has its own unique assets, such as a Scripting API and Thing Descriptions, that need to be protected and also have security and privacy implications.</p>",
    "title": "Web of Things (WoT) Security and Privacy Guidelines",
    "shortname": "wot-security",
    "editor-draft": "https://w3c.github.io/wot-security/",
